$ muster logs --help
Print a process's output log, kept across its runs and after it exits

Usage: muster logs [OPTIONS] [NAME]

Arguments:
  [NAME]  The process, as `muster ps` lists it; quote a name with spaces. Chosen from a list at a terminal when absent

Options:
  -c, --config <CONFIG>  The project's muster.yml. Process commands default to $MUSTER_PROJECT, then ./muster.yml, then the first registered project
  -f, --follow           Keep printing what the process writes, across restarts, until interrupted
      --screen           Print the process's current terminal screen instead of its log
      --json             Print the result as JSON; with --follow, one JSON object per log line
  -h, --help             Print help


$ muster attach --help
Show a running process in this terminal and type into it

Usage: muster attach [OPTIONS] [NAME]

Arguments:
  [NAME]  The process, as `muster ps` lists it; quote a name with spaces. Chosen from a list at a terminal when absent

Options:
  -c, --config <CONFIG>  The project's muster.yml. Process commands default to $MUSTER_PROJECT, then ./muster.yml, then the first registered project
      --read-only        Watch without typing into the process or resizing it
      --json             Print a refusal or failure as JSON; an attach prints nothing else
  -h, --help             Print help (see more with '--help')


$ muster agent --help
Open, close or reopen agent sessions

Usage: muster agent [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  new     Open and start a new agent session
  close   Close an agent session, stopping its process
  reopen  Reopen the most recently closed agent session
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -c, --config <CONFIG>  The project's muster.yml. Process commands default to $MUSTER_PROJECT, then ./muster.yml, then the first registered project
  -h, --help             Print help


$ muster agent new --help
Open and start a new agent session

Usage: muster agent new [OPTIONS] <TOOL>

Arguments:
  <TOOL>  The agent to run; `custom` runs the agent --command names [possible values: claude, codex, gemini, amp, opencode, copilot, kimi, custom]

Options:
  -c, --config <CONFIG>    The project's muster.yml. Process commands default to $MUSTER_PROJECT, then ./muster.yml, then the first registered project
      --name <NAME>        Its name; generated from the agent when absent
      --command <COMMAND>  The command that starts the agent. Required for `custom`; for a preset it replaces the default command
      --resume <TEMPLATE>  The command that resumes a closed conversation. Put `{session_id}` where the agent's conversation id belongs, as a whole unquoted word; without it the id is appended
      --json               Print the result as JSON
  -h, --help               Print help


