$ muster service --help
Show or stop the muster service. Processes keep running either way

Usage: muster service [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  status  Show whether the service runs, its version and what it has loaded, without starting it
  stop    Stop the service. Every process keeps running under its holder, and the next muster command starts the service again
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -c, --config <CONFIG>  The project's muster.yml. Process commands default to $MUSTER_PROJECT, then ./muster.yml, then the first registered project
  -h, --help             Print help


