$ muster run --help
Register a command in a project, start it and attach to it

Usage: muster run [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>...

Arguments:
  <COMMAND>...  The command to register and run, e.g. `-- npm run dev`

Options:
  -c, --config <CONFIG>    The project's muster.yml. Process commands default to $MUSTER_PROJECT, then ./muster.yml, then the first registered project
  -p, --project <PROJECT>  Project to add the command to (a registered project name). Defaults to the current project when run inside a process muster started
  -n, --name <NAME>        Name for the process. Defaults to the command's first word
      --json               Print the report as JSON
  -k, --kind <KIND>        How the process is grouped and managed [default: command] [possible values: agent, terminal, command]
  -h, --help               Print help (see more with '--help')


