$ muster mcp --help
Serve this project to agents as an MCP server over stdio: its processes, agent sessions and shared coordination state (spawned as a child process by a connecting agent)

Usage: muster mcp [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -c, --config <CONFIG>  The project's muster.yml. Process commands default to $MUSTER_PROJECT, then ./muster.yml, then the first registered project
      --print-config     Print the JSON config snippet to add muster to an agent's MCP servers, then exit instead of serving
      --as <NAME>        Identity this server stamps on coordination writes (the connecting agent's name), so entries are attributable. Defaults to a generic agent label
  -h, --help             Print help


